  <p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;">&#160;</p>
  <p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"><sup style="vertical-align:top;line-height:120%;">(1)&#160;&#160;&#160;</sup>Includes loans held-for-sale.</p>
  <p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"><sup style="vertical-align:top;line-height:120%;">(</sup><sup style="vertical-align:top;line-height:120%;">2</sup><sup style="vertical-align:top;line-height:120%;">)</sup><sup style="vertical-align:top;line-height:120%;">&#160;&#160;&#160;</sup>Interest rate spread represents the difference between the average yield on interest-earning assets and the average rate on interest-bearing liabilities.</p>
  <p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; text-indent: -18pt;"><sup style="vertical-align:top;line-height:120%;">(</sup><sup style="vertical-align:top;line-height:120%;">3</sup><sup style="vertical-align:top;line-height:120%;">) &#160;&#160;</sup>Net interest margin represents income before the provision for credit&#160;losses&#160;divided&#160;by&#160;average interest-earning assets.</p>
  <p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"><sup style="vertical-align:top;line-height:120%;">(</sup><sup style="vertical-align:top;line-height:120%;">4</sup><sup style="vertical-align:top;line-height:120%;">) &#160;&#160;</sup>For purposes of this table, tax exempt income is not calculated on a tax equivalent basis.</p>
  <p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;">&#160;</p>
  <p style="margin: 0pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;">Net Interest Margin ("NIM"). Net interest margin for the year ended&#160;December 31, 2025&#160;was 3.92%, an increase of 50&#160;basis points compared to&#160;December 31, 2024. The change in NIM reflects the increase in yields on interest-earning assets and the decrease in the average rate on interest-bearing liabilities.&#160;</p>
  <p style="margin: 0pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;">&#160;</p>
  <div class="PGBK" style="width: 100%; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt;">
   <div class="PGFTR" style="width: 100%; text-align: center;">
